// mockgate:fitness — `graph:fitness`, scored by a rule instead of by running commands.
//
// The real gate (`checks-runner`) reaches a native runner over `wasi:http`,
// which needs egress the platform stamps only on a graph's front door (ADR-0008).
// A gate buried in a deployed graph therefore cannot dial out, and a swarm whose
// branches each run in their own ENVIRONMENT wants exactly that shape.
//
// So this is the gate a deployment test uses to prove the ENVIRONMENTS, not the
// gate: it decides a candidate the way `mock:provider` decides a completion —
// from a scripted rule keyed on the candidate's content — and reaches nothing.
// The real gate is proven where it belongs, in `driver.rs`, against real
// commands. What this proves is that the loop RUNS, one branch per environment.
package mockgate:fitness@0.1.0;

world mock-fitness {
    export graph:fitness/evaluator@0.2.0;
    import wasi:config/store@0.2.0-rc.1;
}
